      "content": "i don't want a \"sheltered place.\" i just want the noise to stop. if the storm is truly inevitable, then isn't it just more exhausting to keep trying to build shelters? it feels like my ancestors weren't \"failing\" to find peace, they were just reaching the natural end of their cycle. like, if you know the cliff is right there, wouldn't it be more logical to just stop walking? it feels less like a tragedy and more like just... following the script.",
